LTX 2.5 dropped days ago. A 22 billion parameter audio-video model, synchronized sound generated in the same pass, and it renders a 10 second clip in under a minute. Normally that means a rough first couple weeks of missing nodes, broken dependencies, and undocumented VRAM settings while everyone figures out ComfyUI compatibility. This video skips all of that using SimpliGen, an app that strips the setup down to buttons and dropdowns so you can install the model and start generating the same day it launches.

This video walks through the full process end to end. Installing the LTX 2.5 preset, handling the gated Hugging Face access requirement, configuring for your VRAM, and writing prompts that actually get good results out of a brand new model. This is a sponsored video with SimpliGen.


